# Storify Code Quality

When writing or reviewing application code (Phase 01+):

## TypeScript & validation

- Keep TypeScript strict; do not weaken `tsconfig` to hide errors.
- Validate all external input (HTTP body/query, webhooks, AI tool args) with explicit schemas.
- Prefer shared domain types over duplicated inline shapes.

## Server authority

- Prices, discounts, tax, inventory availability, and payment amounts are **server-authoritative**.
- Never trust client-supplied monetary values for checkout.
- Never authorize using client-supplied `user_id`, `store_id`, or `organization_id` alone.

## Service role & secrets

- Service-role Supabase keys: server-only, never `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, never client components.
- Prefer user-scoped clients + RLS for user data; service role only for trusted server jobs (e.g. verified webhooks).

## Errors & observability

- Return stable error codes to clients; do not leak secrets or stack traces in production responses.
- Log with request/correlation IDs where available; never log secret values.

## Testing

- New commerce/auth/payment behavior needs tests matching acceptance criteria.
- RLS and webhook signature behavior require automated coverage when touched.

## UX quality

- Loading, empty, and error states required for user-facing flows.
- Accessibility and mobile responsiveness are part of Definition of Done.
- Do not hardcode a single tenant identity in application logic.

## Docs

- Update architecture/status docs when behavior or contracts change.
- Follow `docs/engineering/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md`.
